5.   General Election - November 3, 2026 - Election Day!

1.   [Back to News and Press Releases](https://www.polkcountyiowa.gov/county-auditor/election/news-and-press-releases/ "Back to News and Press Releases")

**Published** 7/16/2026 08:46:47 AM

The general election is held in even-numbered years to elect federal, state, county and township officers. Constitutional amendments and public measures for cities and counties may also be on the ballot.

## Election Day Registration [](https://www.polkcountyiowa.gov/county-auditor/election/news-and-press-releases/general-election-november-3-2026-election-day/#Election%20Day%20Registration)

Voters needing to change their address or register to vote can do so at the [polling place](https://apps.sos.iowa.gov/elections/voterreg/pollingplace/search.aspx "Find Your Polling Place")for their new address.

Election Day Registrants will need to show**proof of identification**_and_**proof of residency**. A valid Iowa driver's license or non-operator ID with the correct address can be used for both.

## Proof of Identity [](https://www.polkcountyiowa.gov/county-auditor/election/news-and-press-releases/general-election-november-3-2026-election-day/#Proof%20of%20Identity)

_(Must include a photo and valid expiration date. An electronic driver's license or non-operator ID will_**_NOT_**_be accepted)._

*   Iowa Driver's License/Non-Operator ID (no more than 90 days expired)

*   Out-of-state driver's license or non-operator ID

*   U.S. Passport

*   U.S. Military or Veteran ID

*   ID card issued by employer

*   High school or college student ID card

*   Tribal ID card or document

*   Iowa Voter Identification Card (must be signed)

## Proof of Residence [](https://www.polkcountyiowa.gov/county-auditor/election/news-and-press-releases/general-election-november-3-2026-election-day/#Proof%20of%20Residence)

_(Must include name and current address and be current within 45 days._**_May be electronic or on paper_**_)._

*   Iowa Driver's License/Non-Operator ID

*   Residential lease

*   Property tax statement

*   Utility bill

*   Bank statement

*   Paycheck/paystub

*   Government check or document

*   Tribal ID or document

## Quick Links [](https://www.polkcountyiowa.gov/county-auditor/election/news-and-press-releases/general-election-november-3-2026-election-day/#Quick%20Links)

